.TH BINARY_DUMP_TO_DTC_FILE 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
binary_dump_to_DTC_file \- convert raw binary data dumps to DTC binary files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B binary_dump_to_DTC_file
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.IR file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
For each input
.IR dir / name
writes
.IR dir /DTC_packets_ name
(truncating any existing file).
The input is a sequence of DMA records, each a 64-bit size word (low 16 bits
used) followed by payload; events that span several DMAs are reassembled,
checked with
.BR DTC_Data_Verifier::VerifyEvent() ,
and written as whole
.B DTC_Event
records.
Reading stops at the first zero-length event.
Does not open any device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Usage, exit 0; an unknown option prints the usage and exits 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0.
An unreadable input is logged
.RB ( "Cannot read file" )
and skipped.
.SH FILES
.IR dir /DTC_packets_ name
\(em output, overwritten without warning.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
binary_dump_to_DTC_file /data/dump/run1234.bin
data_file_verifier /data/dump/DTC_packets_run1234.bin
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR data_file_verifier (1),
.BR DTC_binary_file_compare (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mu2e TDAQ group (Eric Flumerfelt, Ryan Rivera, Ron Rechenmacher and others).
